.TH MYGREP 1 "September 2026" "libmyutils 1.0" "Library Functions"
.SH NAME
mygrep \- search a file for lines containing a pattern
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "myfilefunctions.h"
.sp
.BI "int mygrep(FILE *" fp ", const char *" search_str ", char ***" matches ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mygrep()
function scans the open file stream
.I fp
line by line, looking for lines that contain the substring
.IR search_str .
Matching lines are collected into a dynamically allocated array of
strings, and a pointer to that array is stored in
.IR matches .
This is a simplified reimplementation of the standard
.BR grep (1)
utility's core matching behavior.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of matching lines found, or \-1 on failure.
